  "body": "## What changed\n\nOne Windows zip layout instead of two, and the workflows/docs call `cargo xtask` directly (#752; maintainer: \"We do not want double code and make this confusing.\").\n\n- **`cargo xtask package [--version X.Y.Z] [--out dist] [--bin-dir <dir>] [--dry-run]`** (new `xtask/src/package.rs`): stages `camcraft-<ver>-win-x64/` with the layout in `release_pack.rs` and writes `camcraft-<ver>-win-x64.zip`. No bump, no commit, no build. Without `--version` it reads `<bin-dir>/post.exe --version`, which is what the old workflow block did. Under Actions it appends `version=`, `stage=` and `zip=` to `$GITHUB_OUTPUT` and `CAMCRAFT_VERSION=` to `$GITHUB_ENV`.\n  - Zip writer: still PowerShell `Compress-Archive`, with no new crate. It uses `pwsh` when that is on PATH, else Windows PowerShell 5.1. The runner has pwsh, which is the same tool the old step used.\n  - Non-Windows: a real run is refused by name, since the zip is the win-x64 package and the other OSes ship from `package-*.sh`. `--dry-run` lists the tree on any host.\n- **`cargo xtask release`**: its zip phase now calls `package::package`; the second copy of the staging/zip code is removed.\n- **release.yml (Windows job)**: the inline \"Assemble portable zip\" PowerShell is replaced by `cargo xtask package --bin-dir target/release --out dist` (step id `zip` kept). The job output `version: ${{ steps.zip.outputs.version }}` and `CAMCRAFT_VERSION` keep their names. The installer step now passes `-Stage \"${{ steps.zip.outputs.stage }}\"`, which is the same directory as installer.ps1's default, now named explicitly. Build, signing, cert cleanup, uploads, triggers and the other jobs are unchanged.\n- **ci.yml / nightly.yml**: `cargo xtask gate batch` / `cargo xtask gate release` (shell bash) replace `./scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier ...`. Triggers and matrices are unchanged (`workflow_dispatch` only), and the header comments are corrected.\n- **scripts/README.md**: the gate section is rewritten around `cargo xtask gate`, with Windows and macOS/Linux examples. The wrappers are mentioned once. The \"push/PR CI\" / \"nightly CI\" wording is fixed, since both workflows are manual-only. There are new \"Decisions\" and \"Portable zip (`cargo xtask package`)\" sections, and the installer and signing text now name `cargo xtask release`.\n- **Process files**: the AGENTS.md fork-sync list (prose and the `git checkout upstream/main -- ...` command) and review-prs step 2d now include `scripts/release.ps1` and `scripts/collect-decisions.ps1` / `.sh`. `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes 8 -> 9. #681 is not posted (that happens at merge).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/752-xtask-package.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 28 passed. New pinning tests in `xtask/src/release_tests.rs`:\n  - `package_parse_takes_its_flags`\n  - `package_dry_run_lists_the_release_yml_tree_on_any_host`\n  - `package_refuses_a_real_zip_off_windows_by_name`\n  - `package_reports_what_github_actions_steps_read`\n  - `package_stages_and_zips_on_windows` (cfg(windows); real stage plus Compress-Archive, then checks that the release cut's zip phase goes through the same function)\n  - The existing `zip_layout_mirrors_release_yml` still pins the staged file list.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. `cargo xtask gate quick --dry-run` plans exactly the xtask unit tests.\n- **Layout evidence (old block vs xtask):** I ran the old workflow block's PowerShell body verbatim (with `$ver = \"0.0.0\"` and the post.exe/GITHUB_* lines removed) under Windows PowerShell 5.1. It ran in a temp folder holding copies of `assets/`, the four docs and fake `target/release/{camcraft-ui,camcraft-cli,post}.exe`. Then I ran `cargo xtask package --version 0.0.0 --bin-dir <that fake dir> --out <temp>/new` on this tree. Results:\n  - staged trees: 85 files each, `diff` of the sorted file lists is empty, and md5 of every file is identical;\n  - zip entries: 86 each (85 files plus the folder entry), and the entry lists are identical.\n- `cargo xtask package --version 0.17.0 --dry-run` on the real tree lists 85 files and writes nothing.\n- YAML: all three workflows parse with PyYAML (`yaml.safe_load`). Triggers are unchanged (release: push tags + workflow_dispatch; ci/nightly: workflow_dispatch). The Windows job's outputs and step list were checked.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **release.yml itself cannot run before a tag.** The next `vX.Y.0` tag is its first run with `cargo xtask package`. No workflow was triggered and no tag was pushed. In particular these were not run: `cargo xtask package` on `windows-latest` under pwsh 7, the GITHUB_OUTPUT/GITHUB_ENV hand-off to the installer and publish steps, and ISCC against the reported stage.\n- ci.yml / nightly.yml were not dispatched (Actions budget).\n- Locally there is no pwsh, so the `pwsh` branch of the zip shell was not run; the 5.1 fallback was.\n- A real `cargo xtask release` was not run.\n\nfork: n/a (canonical repo)\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #752\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
